<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net6.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ApplicationIcon />
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <StartupObject />
    <Version>1.8.0</Version>
    <Description>
	  1.8.0
      - All Consul secret encrypt/decrypt logic (ACL token, Basic Auth, whole-document, field-level) extracted to the shared Carbon.ConsulSecretEncryptor.Core library (also used by Carbon.WebApplication and the Carbon.ConsulSecretEncryptor CLI/Windows Forms tools); this project no longer contains any local crypto logic, only env-var wiring and host-pipeline integration.
      - Consul-sourced JSON configuration can now be encrypted at two granularities, usable together: (1) whole-document, as a single "CarbonEncryptedConfig" key, or (2) field-level, as individual "ENC(&lt;base64 envelope&gt;)" values that leave the rest of the structure readable. Both use the same hybrid envelope (random AES-256-GCM key encrypting the value, that key wrapped with RSA-OAEP/SHA256 against the same certificate as the ACL token/Basic Auth) so there is no size limit per value. Decrypted and merged into configuration in place automatically (before any options binding) and re-checked on every Consul reload-on-change; resolving the decryption certificate is only required if either is actually present. See Carbon.ConsulSecretEncryptor --mode json / --mode field to produce the envelopes.
      - Consul HTTP Basic Auth support added for deployments where Consul sits behind a reverse proxy (e.g. nginx) that enforces Basic Auth. Configured via a single CONSUL_BASIC_AUTH_ENCRYPTED variable (RSA-OAEP/SHA256 ciphertext, base64) that decrypts to a "username:password" value, decrypted the same way as the Consul ACL token using the certificate located via CONSUL_ACL_CERT_THUMBPRINT/CONSUL_ACL_CERT_SUBJECT; neither the username nor the password is ever stored in the environment as plaintext.
	  1.7.0
      - Consul ACL token support added. The token is supplied via CONSUL_ACL_TOKEN_ENCRYPTED (RSA-OAEP/SHA256 ciphertext, base64) and decrypted at startup using the private key of a certificate installed on the host, located via CONSUL_ACL_CERT_THUMBPRINT or CONSUL_ACL_CERT_SUBJECT (optional CONSUL_ACL_CERT_STORE_LOCATION/CONSUL_ACL_CERT_STORE_NAME); the plaintext token is never stored in the environment.
      - Consul long-poll (watch) traffic can now be tuned/disabled via CONSUL_RELOAD_ON_CHANGE (default true) and CONSUL_POLL_WAIT_TIME_SECONDS.
	  1.6.1
      - Replaced #if DEBUG compile-time check with a runtime ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development check in UseFeatures.
	  1.6.0
      - .NET 10 (net10.0) target framework added; existing targets preserved.
	  1.5.1
      - Carbon.Common version update
      1.5.0
      - Dotnet 8.0 target framework added, older versions removed
      1.4.0
      - Carbon.Serilog added and Serilog.Enrichers.Sensitive Enricher added for masking sensitive values within logs.
      1.3.3
      - Carbon.Common updated and IQueryable OrderBy extension method bug fixed
      1.3.2
      - Carbon.Common updated and nested ordering achieved
      1.3.1
      - Minor code refactorings, typos
      1.3.0
      - Multiple Consul Support Added, File Config support added for Kubernetes Apps
      1.2.0
      - Serilog.Sinks.ElasticSearch package removed.Reason =&amp;gt; ElasticSearch.Net Dependency problem for 7.x update of ElasticSearch.
          note : add if your app uses ElasticSearch for logging
</Description>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net6.0' or '$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration" Version="3.1.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.EnvironmentVariables" Version="3.1.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting" Version="3.1.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog.AspNetCore" Version="3.2.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog.Sinks.Console" Version="3.1.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog.Sinks.File" Version="4.1.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.ProtectedData" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Winton.Extensions.Configuration.Consul" Version="3.0.1" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration" Version="10.0.9" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.EnvironmentVariables" Version="10.0.9" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting" Version="10.0.9" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog.AspNetCore" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog.Sinks.Console" Version="6.1.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog.Sinks.File" Version="7.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.ProtectedData" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Winton.Extensions.Configuration.Consul" Version="3.0.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Carbon.Common\Carbon.Common.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Carbon.Serilog\Carbon.Serilog.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Carbon.ConsulSecretEncryptor.Core\Carbon.ConsulSecretEncryptor.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
